## Critical: QUpload Syntax Validator Compatibility

All plugins deployed via QUpload are validated using `token_get_all($content, TOKEN_PARSE)` before activation. The following patterns MUST be avoided.

### BLOCKED Patterns (Never Use)

| Pattern | Replacement |
|---------|-------------|
| `is_array($var)` | `gettype($var) === 'array'` |
| `is_string($var)` | `gettype($var) === 'string'` |
| `is_int($var)` | `gettype($var) === 'integer'` |
| `is_float($var)` | `gettype($var) === 'double'` |
| `is_bool($var)` | `gettype($var) === 'boolean'` |
| `is_object($var)` | `gettype($var) === 'object'` |
| `is_null($var)` | `gettype($var) === 'NULL'` |
| `array()` constructor | Use `[]` short syntax |

### SAFE Patterns

`in_array()`, `array_merge()`, `array_filter()`, `array_map()`, `array_key_exists()` — all safe (tokenize as T_STRING).

---

## PHP Coding Rules

- Catch `Throwable`, never `Exception`
- Positive boolean names only (`$isValid`, `$hasData`)
- Extract ternary conditions to named booleans
- Use short array syntax `[]` everywhere

---

## Version Bumping

Any code change bumps at least minor version.

